 "agent": {
  "_doc": "Vehicles. Lamp colours: head_glow a halogen headlamp bulb, a black body at 3200 K (Philips H4 standard bulb); tail_glow the corner of UNECE R48 §2.30 red (y <= 0.335, z <= 0.008: x 0.657, y 0.335); sign_glow the middle of R48 amber (0.398 <= y <= 0.429 on z = 0.007), each from CIE 1931 (Wyman, Sloan & Shirley 2013 fit) to sRGB, out-of-gamut parts clipped, the brightest channel at 1. brake_ratio: a stop lamp at least 5 times its rear position lamp (UNECE R7 §6.2.4.2). Roughness (physicallybased.info): paint 0 (Car Paint: clear topcoat), lens 0 for lamps, signs and the far level's glass (Plastic (PC), Glass), skin 0.5 (Skin I-VI), helmet 0 (Plastic (PC) shell), trim 0.7 (Tire) for every unpainted part, cloth 1 (a matte textile: the database has none). head_power, tail_power, sign_power: how bright the lit lamps draw, set on the night photo (05_transito at 10_noite): a lamp's brightest channel at the top of the display range without bleeding into its body.",
  "shader": "res://render/shaders/agents.gdshader",
  "params": {
   "head_glow": "#ffbf7a",
   "tail_glow": "#ff0000",
   "head_power": 4.0,
   "tail_power": 1.5,
   "brake_ratio": 5.0,
